// Each row is an original editorial brief: title, cluster, answer, record fields,
// interpretation boundary, and the question that closes the handoff.
const rows = [
['First-frost closing records: four things to keep separate','pool-opening-closing','A closing record is easier to check when water readings, debris observations, cover condition, and equipment work have separate entries. A single photograph marked closed leaves the next technician guessing.','Dated water-test record;Accessible debris observations;Cover identity and visible condition;Equipment-specific completion notes','A regional first-frost reminder is not a forecast for the property. Record the local forecast source and let the exact equipment instructions govern the work.','Which closing tasks remain open, who owns them, and where is their completion evidence?'],
['Leaf load before the cover: record the starting condition','pool-opening-closing','Separate what was present on arrival from what was documented at departure. Paired views help a later reader distinguish a changed condition from an incomplete record.','Arrival overview;Visible leaf accumulation;Accessible basket observations;Departure overview','A photograph of a clean surface does not establish water quality or hidden plumbing condition. Do not label the entire pool ready from that image alone.','Which areas could not be observed, and does the next visit need access to them?'],
['Storm preparation: make the equipment handoff readable','field-documentation','Write the storm handoff before access becomes difficult. Identify the equipment, the responsible contact, and the location of its instructions so nobody has to infer a procedure from an old message.','Equipment inventory;Current local alert link;Qualified service contact;Outstanding access issues','This is an information checklist, not a shutdown or restart procedure. Do not approach flooded or otherwise unsafe equipment to obtain a photo.','Who will decide whether the site is safe to enter and equipment can be assessed?'],
['Desert scale complaints: preserve observations before labels','troubleshooting-reference','Describe where a deposit appears and preserve the associated readings before calling it a failed component. A location-specific record is more useful to support than the word scale by itself.','Deposit location;Dated test results;Surface or component identity;Recent maintenance history','Appearance alone does not establish deposit chemistry or justify a cleaner. Avoid applying a surface treatment based on a photo classification.','What evidence does the qualified reviewer need before recommending a surface-specific response?'],
['Spa turnover: a record beyond clear water','spa-hot-tubs','A turnover handoff should connect the last documented service with the next operator. Keep test results and cleaning records distinct from a guest-facing appearance check.','Last completed service;Recorded readings and units;Known use period;Open maintenance items','Clear-looking water is not a substitute for the applicable operating checks. This note does not set treatment amounts or reopening criteria.','Who is responsible for the next required check and the release-to-use decision?'],
['Rain and covered pools: document the drainage question','covers-safety-equipment','Start a rain-related cover inquiry with the cover model, visible accumulation, and the intended drainage destination. These details let the manufacturer and local authority answer different parts of the question.','Cover identity;Observation time;Accessible overview;Proposed discharge destination','Do not walk onto a cover or treat a drainage destination as permitted without checking local requirements. Photographs do not establish load capacity.','Which manufacturer instruction and local discharge guidance apply to this setup?'],
['Public-pool closure references: build a usable source card','facility-cpo','A closure reference card needs an authority, edition, and contact route. Keep a place for the applicable requirement instead of copying a threshold from another facility.','Authority contact;Applicable document edition;Relevant section locator;Escalation owner','General reference material is not proof of the locally adopted rule. A blank or disputed requirement needs resolution by the responsible operator or authority.','Who confirms the current closure and reopening requirements for this venue?'],
['Salt-cell season-end notes before a replacement request','salt-chemistry-controllers','Keep the cell identity, controller identity, and displayed condition together. A replacement discussion becomes ambiguous when a close-up loses the context of the system that produced the alert.','Cell model label;Controller model;Exact displayed message;Service history','A deposit or alert photograph does not prove the cell requires replacement. Cleaning and storage decisions belong to the matching manufacturer instructions.','Which manual revision and support response explain the next verification step?'],
['Pump replacement in California: questions for the counter','pumps-motors','Clarify whether the request concerns a complete pump, motor, or another component before asking about requirements. Preserve the supplier answer with the exact model it addresses.','Existing pump label;Motor label;Proposed replacement identifier;Installer or authority question','This checklist does not interpret California law or certify a replacement. Ask the relevant authority and qualified installer about the specific job.','Does the written answer cover this component, installation, and current requirement?'],
['Safety-cover photographs before a condition review','covers-safety-equipment','An overview and a labeled detail answer different questions. Show where a visible concern sits relative to the cover while preserving the cover identity for support.','Cover identification;Accessible perimeter overview;Concern location;Previous service record','Do not tension, load, or dismantle a cover to improve a photograph. A photo record cannot certify the cover or anchors as safe.','Which observations should go to the cover manufacturer or qualified installer?'],
['Still-open pools: carry readings into the fall handoff','field-documentation','A seasonal handoff should preserve the measurement history and who took each reading. A label such as winter schedule should not erase the conditions behind an operating decision.','Measurement dates;Units and test method;Recent operating changes;Next responsible person','This record does not prescribe a testing interval or chemical adjustment. Keep the facility requirements and product instructions attached to the decision.','What changes require review before the next routine visit?'],
['Robot storage: match the cleaner and power supply','robots-cleaners','Record the cleaner and its power equipment as separate identified items. A storage question can be answered incorrectly when only the marketing family name is available.','Cleaner model;Power supply or charger model;Manual revision;Planned storage location','No storage temperature or charging interval is universal here. Retrieve instructions for the exact cleaner and battery configuration.','Does the storage instruction explicitly cover this model and power equipment?'],
['After flooding: a remote equipment information packet','field-documentation','An initial flood-related packet can use existing records without sending someone into an unsafe area. State which information predates the event and which observations are new.','Last known equipment inventory;Event timeline;Safe remote observations;Qualified contact details','Do not enter floodwater, touch affected equipment, or energize it for documentation. A pre-event photograph is not evidence of present condition.','Who is authorized to assess access and the affected equipment?'],
['Closing appointments: write the access agreement','buyer-proof','An appointment note should distinguish customer preparation from work the service company agreed to perform. Explicit boundaries reduce ambiguity when the crew reaches a locked or obstructed site.','Access arrangement;Agreed service scope;Known obstructions;Customer contact window','Avoid promising a completed close before access and equipment-specific work are confirmed. Store gate codes privately, never in a public article or shared photo.','What happens to the appointment if the agreed access is unavailable?'],
['Exposed equipment before cold weather: an inventory','pool-opening-closing','An annotated equipment inventory helps a qualified technician locate the components discussed in a cold-weather plan. Number observations on a safe overview rather than using ambiguous directions.','Equipment overview;Component labels;Existing protection-plan reference;Unresolved location questions','An inventory is not a freeze-protection design. Do not infer that a component is protected because it is near a running pump.','Which components still lack a verified instruction in the site plan?'],
['Public-spa log handoffs during occupancy changes','facility-cpo','Record the shift boundary and the next responsible operator when occupancy changes. A complete handoff includes unresolved issues as well as the most recent readings.','Shift times;Recorded readings;Recent completed service;Unresolved operator actions','This note does not set operating limits or approve continued use. The responsible operator follows current venue requirements.','Has the incoming operator acknowledged the open items and required next checks?'],
['Vinyl-liner closing records: keep builder instructions attached','pool-opening-closing','Preserve the pool and cover instructions with the closing record. A later reviewer should see what document informed the work without guessing from a generic checklist.','Pool or builder record;Cover model;Applicable instructions;Dated completion record','This article gives no water-level target or winterizing procedure. Those decisions require instructions applicable to the actual pool and cover.','Which document governs this pool when general advice conflicts with its instructions?'],
['Visible algae complaints: write what was actually seen','troubleshooting-reference','Describe the location and timing of a visible complaint before assigning a cause. Include recent measurements so support can distinguish an observation from an interpretation.','Affected location;Observation time;Recorded test results;Recent changes','Do not diagnose an organism or recommend an additive from appearance alone. Keep treatment decisions outside the photo note.','What additional measurements or assessment does the responsible professional request?'],
['Closing plugs at the parts counter: build the request','partsnap','A useful plug inquiry includes markings, the receiving component identity, and existing measurements. Keep similar-looking candidates separate until the supplier confirms the applicable part information.','Receiving equipment model;Existing markings;Available dimensions;Supplier response','Appearance and an approximate diameter do not establish thread compatibility. Do not trial-force an unknown component to test a guess.','What documented part reference supports the proposed replacement?'],
['Chemical storage records during temperature changes','field-documentation','Keep the product label and safety information identifiable when raising a storage question. Record the storage concern without opening containers or moving incompatible materials for a photograph.','Product name;Readable label reference;Observed concern;Trained handler contact','This is a documentation prompt, not a storage design or spill-response procedure. Use the product information and site emergency plan.','Which trained person will resolve the storage concern using the applicable instructions?'],
['Debris after a storm: separate cleanup from equipment review','field-documentation','A storm packet should separate site access, debris observations, and equipment assessment. This prevents a completed cleanup item from being mistaken for authorization to restart equipment.','Safe site overview;Observed debris locations;Equipment assessment status;Responsible trade contacts','Do not treat a cleared path as evidence that electrical or mechanical equipment is ready to use. Record assessment status explicitly.','Which items remain unassessed after the cleanup work?'],
['Above-ground closing: identify the pool and cover together','pool-opening-closing','Record the pool model and cover type in the same closing packet. A cover description alone leaves out the structure and instructions the service work must address.','Pool identification;Cover identification;Builder instructions;Visible condition notes','Do not infer support loads, water levels, or cable settings from this checklist. Use the applicable instructions and qualified judgment.','Are the closing instructions intended for this exact pool-and-cover combination?'],
['Heat-pump complaints: preserve operating context','heaters-heat-pumps','Write down when the complaint occurred, what the display showed, and what the customer expected. A support request is more useful when observed conditions are distinct from desired performance.','Unit model;Displayed message;Observation time and weather source;Requested use','This record does not diagnose a flow, refrigerant, or electrical issue. Do not open equipment or change controls solely to collect evidence.','Which conditions does the manufacturer need to evaluate this complaint?'],
['Controller schedule screenshots before seasonal review','automation-controls','Capture the current schedule and controller clock in the same record before a qualified review. Label the equipment each schedule entry is intended to control.','Controller identity;Clock and timezone display;Schedule screenshots;Recent approved changes','A screenshot records settings, not proof that equipment follows them. Avoid changing freeze or safety-related settings from general advice.','Who will verify the intended schedule against actual equipment behavior?'],
['Filter pressure history for the closing packet','filters-valves-plumbing','Preserve the reading with its operating context, not as a number alone. A later reviewer needs to know whether two recorded readings describe comparable conditions.','Filter model;Gauge reading and units;Recorded operating state;Service date','This note sets no pressure threshold and instructs no opening or service of a vessel. Use the filter instructions for any intervention.','Are the compared readings from equivalent documented operating conditions?'],
['Customer closing signoff: separate completion and exceptions','buyer-proof','A useful signoff lists completed work and unresolved exceptions separately. Attach the supporting record to each statement rather than asking the customer to approve a vague all-done summary.','Agreed scope;Completion evidence;Exceptions;Next contact date','Acknowledgment of a report does not create a warranty or waive a safety concern. Preserve the wording of the actual agreement.','Which unresolved items were acknowledged and assigned to someone?'],
['A freeze alert and the site plan: keep both timestamps','pool-opening-closing','Save the alert issue time and the site plan revision separately. A forecast changes; the record should show which information was available when the responsible person reviewed the plan.','Alert source and time;Site plan revision;Equipment inventory;Review contact','A regional alert is not a site-specific equipment instruction. Do not copy a forecast screenshot without its location and timestamp.','Who will recheck the current alert and the applicable site plan?'],
['Heater display codes: transcribe before interpreting','heaters-heat-pumps','Preserve the exact characters, unit identity, and observation time before looking up a message. Similar labels can refer to different equipment families or document revisions.','Full unit label;Exact display text;Time observed;Official manual locator','A matching code string does not establish the cause or authorize a repair. Keep manufacturer troubleshooting with the qualified service provider.','Does the reference explicitly match this model and displayed message?'],
['Cover-pump inquiries: include the destination question','covers-safety-equipment','Keep equipment suitability and water discharge permission as separate questions. A device manual cannot answer every local drainage issue for the property.','Device model;Cover instructions;Proposed destination;Local authority contact','Do not assume that water may enter a street drain. This note does not direct pumping or electrical setup.','Who confirms both equipment suitability and the permitted discharge route?'],
['Warm-weekend pool use after the closing visit','pool-opening-closing','When plans change, start with the recorded closing status rather than assuming the pool can return to use. Identify what the service company completed and who can assess the changed request.','Closing date;Completed work;Customer requested change;Qualified contact','A warm forecast does not reverse winterizing work or establish readiness for swimmers. Avoid informal restart instructions.','Who will evaluate the requested change against the documented closing work?'],
['Spare-part packaging: keep labels with the actual part','buyer-proof','Photograph the part and its packaging as associated but separate evidence. A box identifier is less useful when nobody can establish whether the enclosed component is the original item.','Part markings;Packaging identifier;Purchase record;Observed mismatch','Packaging alone does not prove authenticity or compatibility. Ask the supplier to resolve mismatches before an installation decision.','Does the supplier confirm the item itself, not just the box label?'],
['Halloween rental turnover: name the next pool contact','spa-hot-tubs','A rental turnover note should give the next responsible contact an unambiguous service status. Distinguish guest observations from checks completed by the service provider.','Service timestamp;Open guest reports;Recorded completion items;Next service contact','A guest checklist is not a public-spa operating approval. Keep access credentials and guest identities out of shared evidence.','Who handles an unresolved report between guest stays?'],
['Daylight-saving time: record controller time before review','automation-controls','Record controller time alongside a trusted current time when investigating a schedule discrepancy. Note whether the display exposes a timezone or daylight-saving setting.','Controller model;Displayed time;Reference time;Affected scheduled function','Do not assume every controller changes clocks automatically. The matching manual and qualified operator should determine the appropriate adjustment.','Is the discrepancy a clock issue, a schedule issue, or still unverified?'],
['Cold-front handoffs when the regular technician is away','field-documentation','A substitute technician needs the current plan, not just the last text message. Provide the equipment inventory and mark decisions that require the usual responsible person.','Current site plan;Equipment identifiers;Outstanding decisions;Backup contact','A substitute handoff does not expand anyone\'s qualifications. Keep electrical, gas, and other restricted work with qualified personnel.','Who can resolve a question the substitute is not authorized to decide?'],
['Heater quote requests: separate comfort goals from evidence','heaters-heat-pumps','Write the requested use pattern separately from the existing equipment facts. This gives the qualified installer a clear question without implying a universal sizing answer.','Existing equipment;Desired use window;Available site records;Installer questions','This record does not size equipment or promise a heat-up time. Performance and installation requirements need a site-specific assessment.','What additional site information is required for a supported proposal?'],
['Manual downloads: label the document before filing it','manuals-sources','Name a stored reference by equipment family, revision, and source URL. A file named manual-final is difficult to trust when several similar models are in the inventory.','Document title;Revision or publication date;Model applicability;Official URL','A downloaded copy may become outdated. Keep the official route so the next reader can check for a newer applicable version.','What confirms that this revision covers the equipment in the record?'],
['Indoor-pool odor reports: keep the report specific','facility-cpo','Record when and where an odor complaint occurred, together with available operating records. Preserve the complainant\'s observation without assigning a chemical or ventilation diagnosis.','Time and location;Exact reported concern;Available readings;Operator follow-up','An odor description cannot determine water chemistry or HVAC performance. Route the concern to the responsible operator and qualified specialists.','Which records will the operator and facility team compare before deciding an action?'],
['Spa cover condition: make the concern locatable','spa-hot-tubs','Tie each visible cover concern to an overview and the cover identity. A close-up without location makes it difficult for support to understand what the customer is describing.','Cover identity;Accessible overview;Concern detail;Service history','Do not stand on, load, or dismantle the cover for the record. This note does not certify insulation, support, or safe use.','Can the manufacturer identify the affected area from the submitted evidence?'],
['Customer freeze questions: record uncertainty explicitly','field-documentation','A useful reply states what is known, what remains unverified, and who will review it. Keep the customer\'s question intact rather than replacing it with an assumed diagnosis.','Exact customer question;Verified equipment details;Missing information;Review owner','Avoid guarantees that a system will withstand an event. Documentation supports a review; it does not provide insurance or freeze protection.','What must be verified before a qualified person can answer the question?'],
['Cartridge identification: capture ends as well as dimensions','filters-valves-plumbing','A cartridge request benefits from the equipment label and existing element markings. Record available dimensions and end configuration as evidence to be checked, not as a substitute for a part reference.','Filter model;Element markings;Available dimensions;End configuration','Similar dimensions alone do not prove interchangeability. Follow the equipment instructions for access and leave pressurized equipment closed.','Which manufacturer part reference confirms the supplier\'s candidate?'],
['Robot accessories: keep model variants distinct','robots-cleaners','List the exact cleaner variant when asking about a basket, cable, or charger. Keep separate candidate part numbers so a conversation cannot silently switch between them.','Cleaner variant;Accessory markings;Candidate identifier;Supplier confirmation','An accessory sold for a product family may not cover every revision. Do not infer electrical compatibility from connector appearance.','Does the written compatibility statement include this exact variant?'],
['Facility relief shifts: write an exception-first handoff','facility-cpo','Put unresolved items at the top of the relief-shift record. The incoming operator should be able to identify decisions still pending without reading the entire service history.','Open exceptions;Latest required records;Responsible contacts;Acknowledgment time','A shift handoff does not replace training or local operating requirements. Do not treat an unread message as an accepted responsibility transfer.','Has the incoming responsible person acknowledged each open action?'],
['Pump and motor labels: do not collapse two identities','pumps-motors','Keep the pump housing and motor labels distinct in a parts inquiry. A replacement decision based on one label may miss the identity of the other assembly.','Pump label;Motor label;Existing part reference;Supplier question','This is not an electrical inspection or a compatibility decision. Do not remove guards or open electrical compartments for identification.','Which assembly does the proposed replacement actually address?'],
['Holiday service scope: document what is excluded','buyer-proof','A holiday service agreement should distinguish the scheduled visit from emergency coverage. Put exceptions beside the scope so the customer can see who to contact outside the planned window.','Scheduled work;Exclusions;Service contact hours;Emergency contact route','Do not imply emergency response or guaranteed availability unless that service is actually offered. Keep the statement consistent with the agreement.','Who handles issues outside the scheduled service scope?'],
['Cover hardware requests: label each candidate','covers-safety-equipment','Use one identifier per hardware candidate and preserve its relation to the cover record. Loose hardware photographs without context make supplier confirmation harder.','Cover model;Existing hardware markings;Candidate reference;Installer question','Visual resemblance does not establish load rating or suitability. A parts conversation is not authorization to modify a cover system.','Which documented reference supports the installer\'s chosen hardware?'],
['Winter leak reports: separate observation from loss estimate','troubleshooting-reference','Record comparable observations and their times before describing a trend. Preserve weather and service context so a reviewer can assess whether the records are comparable.','Observation times;Consistent reference point;Recent service;Weather context','A changing level alone does not identify a leak location or cause. Do not direct draining or invasive testing from this record.','What additional comparison does the qualified assessor need?'],
['Spa water-replacement questions: keep use history available','spa-hot-tubs','Keep the last documented water service and available use history together when asking about replacement timing. The record should show missing information instead of assuming a standard interval.','Last service record;Available use history;Operator requirements;Current concern','This note sets no replacement frequency or treatment method. Use applicable facility requirements and exact product instructions.','Which requirement or manufacturer instruction governs this specific spa?'],
['Storm-season closeout: preserve unresolved assessments','field-documentation','A seasonal recap should distinguish completed assessments from unresolved concerns. Closing the calendar period should not silently mark equipment issues complete.','Event timeline;Completed assessments;Unresolved concerns;Assigned follow-up','The end of a season does not establish that affected equipment is ready for use. Keep assessment status separate from cleanup status.','Which unresolved concern still needs an authorized assessment?'],
['Salt-system winter notes: identify more than the cell','salt-chemistry-controllers','Keep controller, cell, and sensor identities together in the winter record. This lets the support contact determine which component a question or display message concerns.','Controller label;Cell label;Sensor identification if accessible;Applicable manual','This note gives no draining, cleaning, or storage sequence. Do not substitute instructions from a similar salt-system family.','Do the stored instructions cover every component named in the winter plan?'],
['Indoor-pool complaints before a busy week','facility-cpo','Connect each reported concern with the time, area, and responsible follow-up contact. Preserve water records and facility observations separately so different specialists can review their evidence.','Complaint timeline;Available operating records;Facility observations;Follow-up owner','Do not infer a chemical or ventilation remedy from a complaint summary. The responsible operator coordinates the qualified review.','Which part of the concern is assigned to the operator and which to the facility team?'],
['Exposed pads in Texas: locate the existing cold-weather plan','pool-opening-closing','Begin a cold-weather inquiry by finding the site\'s current plan and equipment inventory. Record gaps before the forecast requires a rushed decision.','Plan revision;Equipment labels;Qualified contact;Unanswered outage questions','This note is not a statewide freeze procedure. A regional label does not determine what a particular installation needs.','Who can resolve the plan\'s equipment-specific gaps before conditions change?'],
['Desert winter readings: preserve the baseline','field-documentation','When seasonal conditions change, retain the prior readings rather than replacing them with a new summary. A dated sequence helps the reviewer see what was actually measured.','Earlier readings;Current readings;Units and method;Recent changes','This article provides no chemistry targets or dosing adjustment. Avoid treating a seasonal assumption as a measurement.','Which recorded change needs interpretation by the responsible professional?'],
['Cartridge orders during a sale: verify before checkout','buyer-proof','Keep the promotional offer separate from the compatibility evidence. Record the proposed item and the source supporting it before an order is approved.','Existing filter model;Current element reference;Offered item identifier;Written compatibility response','A discount or retailer category is not proof of fit. Do not let a sale deadline replace the missing source check.','Who confirms the item reference before the purchase is authorized?'],
['Emergency-control records: document the inspection route','facility-cpo','An emergency-control record should identify the device, the governing inspection process, and who completed the documented check. Keep an observation separate from a functional test.','Device location;Applicable procedure;Qualified inspection record;Open issues','Do not operate or test emergency equipment from this article. Follow the venue process and authorized personnel\'s instructions.','Where is the current authorized inspection record and its unresolved actions?'],
['Rental arrivals: distinguish service status from guest notes','spa-hot-tubs','A guest-arrival packet should present the actual service status and the correct reporting contact. Keep guest observations separate from operator decisions.','Latest completed service;Open concerns;Guest reporting route;Responsible operator','A guest message cannot approve water quality or equipment readiness. Do not expose private service access details in guest materials.','Who receives and acts on a guest report during the stay?'],
['An idle heater: build the service request before startup','heaters-heat-pumps','Include the last known use and recorded service history when requesting an idle-heater assessment. Distinguish customer recollection from dated maintenance evidence.','Unit identity;Last documented use;Service history;Current visible display','This note does not authorize startup or inspection inside the unit. Gas and electrical work require qualified personnel and the exact instructions.','What records does the qualified service provider need before assessing the heater?'],
['Chemical-room holiday coverage: make the contacts usable','facility-cpo','A coverage note should identify trained responsible people and the location of approved emergency information. Test that the contact route is understood before routine staffing changes.','Responsible roles;Coverage times;Safety information location;Emergency contact route','This record does not train a chemical handler or supply a spill procedure. Follow the site plan and applicable product safety information.','Who owns the response when the regular trained person is unavailable?'],
['Pre-holiday spa records: avoid an appearance-only signoff','spa-hot-tubs','Use the actual completed checks in the handoff instead of a photograph labeled clear. Preserve who recorded each result and when.','Completed check record;Observation timestamp;Responsible person;Outstanding requirements','A clear photograph cannot establish operating suitability. The responsible operator follows the applicable release-to-use requirements.','What required check remains incomplete before the operator makes a decision?'],
['Holiday operations: name the next required check','facility-cpo','For facilities that remain open, record the next responsible person and required check explicitly. A holiday date should not obscure the handoff between shifts.','Applicable checking requirements;Assigned coverage;Last recorded check;Open incidents','This note does not set a testing cadence. Use the venue\'s current requirements and authorized operating procedures.','Who has accepted responsibility for the next required check?'],
['After a busy stay: record the complaint before treatment','spa-hot-tubs','Separate guest reports, observed conditions, and measured results in the post-stay packet. That separation makes it easier to ask a precise service question.','Guest concern without identity;Observed condition;Recorded results;Last service','This note recommends no chemical dose or universal recovery procedure. Avoid converting a guest description directly into a treatment instruction.','Which observations still need verification by the responsible service provider?'],
['Covered-pool complaints after rain: a comparison record','pool-opening-closing','Compare the current accessible overview with the closing record and label the dates. State which covered areas could not be observed.','Closing overview;Current accessible view;Dates and weather context;Unobservable areas','A covered-pool photograph cannot establish the entire pool\'s condition. Do not remove or load a cover to satisfy this checklist.','Which change warrants an assessment by the cover or pool service professional?'],
['Before heavy snow: document safe observation points','covers-safety-equipment','A cover-observation plan should identify safe viewpoints and the professional contact for concerns. Use existing manufacturer information to frame the questions.','Cover identity;Accessible viewpoint;Visible concern;Installer contact','Do not walk onto a cover or ice, or infer snow-load capacity from appearance. This article provides no snow-removal procedure.','Which concern should be referred to the cover manufacturer before any intervention?'],
['Storm recovery recap: keep the open items visible','field-documentation','A recovery recap is most useful when it lists what remains unresolved. Tie completed work to dated evidence so a reader can distinguish work performed from work requested.','Completed work records;Outstanding assessments;Responsible contacts;Next review date','Do not replace a qualified assessment with a recap statement. A tidy report does not certify equipment condition.','Which unfinished action must remain visible in the next service record?'],
['December route reset: compare planned and actual visits','field-documentation','Review whether the visit record still reflects the actual service scope. Separate recurring observations from equipment-specific work that needs a separate appointment.','Current scope;Recent visit records;Unresolved equipment items;Customer expectations','This note sets no winter operating schedule or chemical requirement. Keep changes to service scope explicit and agreed.','Which items belong in routine documentation and which need a qualified service booking?'],
['Pump-efficiency discussions: gather the comparison inputs','pumps-motors','A useful efficiency discussion begins with equipment identity and documented operating information. Keep a proposed change separate from an unverified savings estimate.','Existing model;Recorded schedule;Relevant utility information;Installer proposal','This article promises no energy savings or payback period. A supported comparison needs an appropriate calculation and current applicable requirements.','What assumptions and source data support the proposed comparison?'],
['Resort-spa season: prepare the shift record','facility-cpo','Make the shift record easy to transfer when staffing or use changes. Put unresolved service issues next to the next responsible person.','Shift coverage;Current operating records;Service exceptions;Escalation contact','This template does not set a testing frequency or occupancy limit. The operator must use the applicable venue requirements.','Who reviews the exceptions before responsibility changes hands?'],
['Freeze-damage conversations: describe observed condition','field-documentation','Keep observations, event timing, and completed work distinct when preparing a damage packet. Preserve original records so a reviewer can see when each statement was made.','Dated observations;Relevant event timeline;Prior condition records;Qualified assessment','This article does not determine cause, coverage, or liability. Avoid labeling damage insured or excluded in a field observation.','What evidence has the insurer or qualified assessor actually requested?'],
['Robot purchase questions: write the use case first','robots-cleaners','List the intended pool and storage context before comparing cleaner candidates. Record the official specification supporting each proposed match.','Pool characteristics supplied by owner;Desired use;Candidate model;Official specification route','This note does not rank products or establish suitability. Marketing descriptions should not replace the specific manufacturer information.','Which candidate claim is documented for the intended use case?'],
['Drain-cover records: route the compliance question','covers-safety-equipment','A drain-cover inquiry should start with the existing installation and inspection records. Keep identity, installation date, and the authority question linked.','Available cover identification;Installation record;Inspection record;Authority contact','Do not enter the water or remove equipment for this checklist. It does not certify compliance or specify a replacement.','Which qualified party will verify the requirements for this exact installation?'],
['Cold-weather indoor-pool reports: separate teams and evidence','facility-cpo','Keep water-operation records and building-system observations in distinct sections of the complaint packet. Assign a contact for each part so one team\'s completed task does not close the other\'s question.','Complaint timing;Operator records;Facility observations;Assigned reviewers','No diagnosis or ventilation adjustment is provided here. Qualified personnel must interpret the evidence for their systems.','What is still unresolved after each team has reviewed its own records?'],
['Apartment-spa operator information: preserve the authority route','facility-cpo','Keep the venue\'s authority contact and applicable operating documents with its staff records. A role title alone does not show which requirements apply.','Venue identity;Authority route;Current operating documents;Assigned operator contact','This article does not determine certification or staffing obligations in Texas or elsewhere. Confirm the actual requirements with the responsible authority.','Who verifies that the staff record matches the venue\'s current obligations?'],
['Winter chemistry records: keep assumptions out of the log','salt-chemistry-controllers','Write the observed reading and its units before adding interpretation. Seasonal expectations belong in a separate note, not in place of the result.','Reading and units;Timestamp;Method or instrument;Interpretation owner','This note sets no sanitizer target or dosing amount. A controller display and an independent reading may require qualified reconciliation.','Who will interpret a disagreement between the recorded sources?'],
['Water-level concerns under a cover: label the limits','covers-safety-equipment','State the observation method and its limitations when reporting water level under a cover. An inaccessible reference point should be marked unknown rather than estimated.','Cover identity;Observation method;Dated comparison;Uncertain details','Do not walk on or remove a cover to obtain a measurement. This article gives no recommended water level.','What safe assessment method does the cover or pool professional recommend?'],
['Heater comparison requests: define the decision inputs','heaters-heat-pumps','Give the installer a use case, existing equipment information, and site constraints before asking for a technology comparison. Keep desired outcomes distinct from verified capabilities.','Intended use;Existing equipment;Known site constraints;Installer questions','This article does not choose gas or heat-pump equipment, size a system, or estimate costs. Those decisions require current site-specific information.','Which missing input prevents the installer from making a supported comparison?'],
['Spa foam reports: collect a timeline without a diagnosis','troubleshooting-reference','Record when the foam appeared and what changed recently. Preserve available service and use history so the professional can ask focused follow-up questions.','First observation;Recent products or service reported;Available readings;Water-service history','Appearance alone cannot establish a cause or justify an additive. This record does not prescribe a treatment.','Which recent change needs verification before the professional interprets the complaint?'],
['Pool drainage inquiries: keep local permission separate','manuals-sources','A drainage packet should identify the proposed water source and destination before asking the local authority. Save the response with the location and date it covers.','Water source;Proposed destination;Jurisdiction contact;Written response','Manufacturer equipment instructions do not establish local discharge permission. Do not treat guidance from another municipality as approval.','Does the response explicitly cover this location and proposed discharge?'],
['Replacement motors: distinguish the item from the installation','pumps-motors','Keep the existing motor, pump assembly, and proposed replacement identified separately. Ask the qualified installer which requirements need confirmation for the actual job.','Motor label;Pump label;Proposed model;Installer or authority response','This note interprets no California rule and gives no wiring instruction. A catalog listing cannot certify the installation.','Which documented answers cover both the replacement item and its intended installation?'],
['Year-end facility records: index before archiving','facility-cpo','Create an index linking each record category to its date range and storage location. Mark missing periods so an orderly folder is not mistaken for a complete record.','Record categories;Covered dates;Missing periods;Responsible custodian','This article specifies no legal retention period. Confirm applicable requirements before deleting or changing access to records.','Who resolves missing records and confirms the applicable retention policy?'],
['Freeze-mode screenshots: settings are not performance proof','automation-controls','Preserve the displayed settings and the controller identity before a qualified review. Add the observation time so a later change can be distinguished from the original state.','Controller model;Settings screenshots;Observation time;Known equipment mapping','A setting does not prove a sensor or connected component works. Do not test protection functions from this article.','Who will verify the displayed configuration against the actual installation?'],
['Cold-water salt alerts: capture the exact message','salt-chemistry-controllers','Transcribe the full displayed message and identify the cell and controller before searching for an explanation. Keep any measured temperature separate from a controller assumption.','Exact display text;Controller model;Cell model;Available temperature record','This note sets no temperature threshold and does not diagnose a failed cell. Use the matching manual and manufacturer support.','Which source explicitly explains the message for this controller revision?'],
['Rule-change questions: save the effective-date evidence','manuals-sources','When someone reports a rule change, preserve the issuing authority, exact document, and effective-date information. A social post or summary is a starting lead, not the controlling text.','Issuing authority;Document title;Effective-date section;Applicability question','This article asserts no new Oregon or other state rule. Resolve adoption and applicability with the responsible authority before changing operations.','Does the published authority text apply to this venue on the relevant date?'],
['Rental-spa information cards: name the source and contact','spa-hot-tubs','A guest information card should identify who to contact and where its approved wording came from. Keep operational decisions with the responsible service or venue staff.','Approved venue wording;Responsible contact;Emergency route;Review date','Do not invent temperature, supervision, or reopening requirements in a generic card. Use the applicable approved instructions.','Who has reviewed this card for the actual property and its operating requirements?'],
['Chemical-feed maintenance records: separate status from action','salt-chemistry-controllers','Record what the maintenance request concerns and which qualified person owns it. Label an observed message differently from a completed inspection or repair.','Equipment model;Observed condition;Applicable manual;Assigned service provider','This checklist gives no feeder service, interlock test, or chemical-handling procedure. Do not open or bypass equipment for documentation.','What evidence is needed to close the service item after authorized work?'],
['Pump-schedule review: preserve the original configuration','pumps-motors','Save the current schedule before discussing a change, together with the equipment it serves. A before-and-after record makes an approved adjustment easier to trace.','Current schedule;Pump model;Known connected functions;Approved change request','This article recommends no speed or runtime. A qualified review must consider the actual installation and applicable requirements.','Which functions and constraints must the reviewer account for before approving a change?'],
['Power-outage planning: make the unresolved questions explicit','pool-opening-closing','Keep the outage contact list and equipment instructions available before a forecast event. Write unanswered equipment questions where the responsible person can see them.','Equipment inventory;Applicable instructions;Backup contact route;Unresolved plan questions','This article gives no emergency draining, rewiring, or restart procedure. Do not improvise around unavailable power or unsafe access.','Who is qualified and authorized to resolve each equipment-specific question?'],
['Spa reopening questions: preserve the governing reference','facility-cpo','A reopening question should identify the event, applicable procedure, and responsible decision-maker. Save the actual evidence required by that procedure instead of relying on a generic elapsed time.','Event record;Applicable procedure;Required completed records;Decision owner','This note gives no treatment amount or waiting period. Reopening remains subject to the applicable requirements and responsible operator.','Which required evidence is still missing before the operator can decide?'],
['Holiday access notes: keep private details private','field-documentation','Write a service handoff that states whether access is confirmed without publishing credentials. Separate customer-facing status from restricted access instructions.','Access confirmation status;Service window;Private credential location;Contact route','Do not put gate codes, customer addresses, or account information into public screenshots or analytics parameters. Use the approved private channel.','Can the assigned technician reach the private instructions without exposing them to others?'],
['No-tool owner observations: report without intervening','field-documentation','A customer can report an accessible visible concern without attempting service. Ask for the observation time, location description, and a safe overview only when access is safe.','Observation time;Visible concern;Safe overview if available;Service contact','Do not open panels, enter unsafe areas, approach chemical incidents, or operate equipment to create a report. Urgent hazards need the appropriate emergency response.','Who should receive the observation and decide the next safe step?'],
['Post-holiday spa handoffs: compare service records','spa-hot-tubs','Connect the pre-holiday service record to the next assessment. Keep reported use and new observations distinct from checks a technician actually completed.','Prior service record;New observations;Reported use context;Pending assessment','This note provides no universal recovery process or treatment. The responsible professional uses the applicable requirements and exact instructions.','Which change since the prior service needs a documented follow-up?'],
['Tile-line deposit inquiries: identify the surface first','troubleshooting-reference','Include the surface identity and the deposit location when asking about cleaning. Unknown surface information should stay unknown until it is verified.','Surface or builder record;Deposit location;Previous treatment history;Professional question','This article recommends no acid, abrasive, or cleaning process. A photograph does not establish material compatibility or cause.','What surface information does the qualified professional require before recommending any treatment?'],
['Year-end parts inventory: separate stock from confirmed fit','buyer-proof','Label inventory with its actual identifier and keep equipment compatibility evidence separately. A familiar shelf location is not a substitute for checking a part request.','Stock item identifier;Quantity record;Manufacturer reference;Unresolved cross-reference','Do not convert a commonly ordered item into a universal replacement. Verify each request against the applicable equipment information.','Which stock entries need source confirmation before the next ordering season?'],
['Facility safety records: distinguish present from inspected','facility-cpo','An inventory can show an item is present without proving it has been inspected. Use separate fields for location, inspection record, and unresolved issue.','Item location;Inspection record date;Responsible inspector;Outstanding issue','This article does not prescribe a safety inspection or certify readiness. Use the authorized venue process and applicable requirements.','Which items lack a current inspection record under the venue\'s process?'],
['Holiday heater expectations: document the request','heaters-heat-pumps','Record the customer\'s desired use time and the existing equipment context before passing the question to service. Keep a requested temperature separate from an observed reading.','Requested use window;Existing model;Observed display;Relevant service history','This note promises no heat-up time or achievable temperature. A qualified assessment needs the actual operating and installation conditions.','What can the service provider confirm, and which expectations remain unverified?'],
['Year-end field notes: choose records worth carrying forward','field-documentation','Carry forward unresolved decisions and the records needed to resolve them. A shorter current index is more useful than copying every old note into a new report.','Open decisions;Relevant source records;Assigned owners;Next review dates','Do not discard originals or apply a retention period from this article. Keep the organization\'s approved record policy.','Can each owner find the evidence behind their next action?'],
['New-year facility logs: preserve continuity','facility-cpo','Start the new log period with a reference to the last completed record and its open items. A fresh template should not reset unresolved maintenance status.','Prior period reference;Open maintenance;Responsible staff;Current document version','This note does not change recordkeeping obligations or operating procedures. Confirm the template with the responsible operator.','Which unresolved item must remain visible across the year boundary?'],
['Winter guest turnover: connect debris reports to service','field-documentation','Record the timing and location of debris reports alongside the service schedule. Separate customer observations from work actually completed.','Report timestamp;Reported area;Service completion record;Next contact','A debris photograph does not establish water quality or equipment performance. Do not infer a chemical adjustment from it.','Which report needs a service assessment before the next guest turnover?'],
['Sudden cold forecasts: record the site-specific questions','pool-opening-closing','Use a current local forecast to identify when the responsible person must review the existing plan. Keep the equipment-specific questions explicit.','Forecast URL and time;Site plan revision;Equipment inventory;Review contact','A regional weather label is not an equipment procedure. Do not substitute general cold-weather advice for the actual installation instructions.','Which unanswered question needs qualified review before conditions change?'],
['Utility-rate questions and pool schedules: collect both records','pumps-motors','Keep the current utility information and equipment schedule as separate inputs to a proposed review. Preserve the source date so old rates are not silently reused.','Utility source and date;Current schedule;Equipment identity;Review assumptions','This article asserts no rate change or savings result. A qualified review must account for equipment needs and applicable constraints.','Which current source supports each assumption in the proposed schedule comparison?'],
['Busy spa season: preserve the service timeline','spa-hot-tubs','A clear timeline helps a service provider distinguish routine maintenance from a new complaint. Record actual dates and identify gaps rather than filling them from memory.','Completed service dates;New concern date;Available operating records;Missing information','This note sets no maintenance frequency, treatment amount, or replacement interval. Use the applicable spa and venue instructions.','Which gap in the timeline matters to the next qualified assessment?'],
['Swim-school operations: make the handoff match the venue','facility-cpo','Keep session context and operational records together without including student identities. The incoming operator should see unresolved service questions and responsible contacts.','Session schedule context;Required operating records;Open service items;Assigned contacts','This article sets no staffing, testing, or supervision requirements. Follow the venue\'s applicable rules and approved procedures.','Which operating question needs resolution before responsibility transfers?'],
['Cover ice concerns: prepare a manufacturer inquiry','covers-safety-equipment','Identify the cover and describe the concern from a safe accessible location. Keep dated observations separate from guesses about ice or load.','Cover model;Observation date;Safe overview;Manufacturer contact','Do not walk on a cover or ice, or attempt removal based on this note. It gives no load rating or intervention procedure.','What does the manufacturer need to advise the qualified service provider?'],
['Cordless-cleaner storage: verify the battery variant','robots-cleaners','Keep the exact cleaner and charger identifiers with the official storage instructions. A general cordless-cleaner tip may refer to a different battery or charging system.','Cleaner model;Charger model;Manual revision;Storage question','This note specifies no charge level, interval, or storage temperature. Do not infer compatibility from a connector or brand family.','Does the official instruction cover this precise cleaner-and-charger combination?'],
['Spring salt-system planning starts with winter records','salt-chemistry-controllers','Connect the closing record to winter observations before requesting opening service. Label issues that were observed separately from work that was completed.','Closing record;Winter observations;Component identifiers;Open service items','This article gives no reinstall or startup sequence. Follow the exact system instructions and qualified service assessment.','Which unresolved item should the opening technician review before planning the work?'],
['Freeze-rain concerns: separate access from equipment','pool-opening-closing','A weather-related service request should state whether access is known to be safe. Existing equipment records can support the inquiry when new photographs are unsafe to obtain.','Current weather source;Known access status;Existing equipment inventory;Qualified contact','Do not enter icy or hazardous areas to complete this record. It does not specify freeze protection or electrical actions.','Who determines safe access before an on-site assessment is attempted?'],
['Chemical-spill training records: document the approved drill','facility-cpo','A drill record should identify the approved exercise, participants\' roles, and follow-up actions. Keep simulated observations visibly separate from real incidents.','Approved drill reference;Participant roles;Observed gaps;Assigned follow-up','This article is not a spill-response procedure. Use the site emergency plan, applicable safety information, and trained personnel.','Which gap needs resolution before the next approved exercise?'],
['Spring bookings: ask for useful existing records','buyer-proof','An opening inquiry should collect the prior closing record and known equipment information before promising a scope. Explain which observations can be supplied safely.','Closing record;Equipment identities;Customer requested scope;Known access constraints','Do not promise readiness or request unsafe inspection to complete a booking. A proposal may need a qualified site assessment.','What information is still needed before the service scope can be confirmed?'],
['Pad-rebuild planning: distinguish observed and proposed','buyer-proof','Keep the existing equipment record separate from proposed changes. Link every requested change to its reason and the professional who will assess it.','Existing inventory;Observed concern;Proposed change;Qualified reviewer','This note is not an installation design or code interpretation. Do not infer that a proposed layout is permitted from an annotated photo.','Which design question must be resolved before a supported quote is prepared?'],
['Inspection-binder review: expose missing records','facility-cpo','An inspection binder needs an index that shows coverage and gaps. Mark an unavailable record honestly instead of replacing it with an undated summary.','Required record list from authority;Available date ranges;Missing records;Responsible custodian','This article does not define Florida or other jurisdiction inspection requirements. Confirm the actual list with the responsible authority.','Which missing record has an assigned owner and a resolution date?'],
['Offseason barrier reports: keep observation and inspection distinct','covers-safety-equipment','Record the accessible visible concern and its location when reporting a barrier issue. Attach the relevant inspection record if one exists.','Concern location;Observation date;Existing inspection record;Responsible contact','Do not represent a visual report as a code inspection or certification. Urgent access hazards need the venue\'s appropriate response.','Who is authorized to inspect and resolve the reported barrier concern?'],
['Acid-wash questions: start with surface information','troubleshooting-reference','Preserve the customer\'s question and the available surface history before asking a qualified specialist. Keep uncertain material information explicit.','Surface records;Reported concern;Previous treatment history;Specialist question','This article recommends no acid treatment or dilution. Surface identification and professional assessment must precede any treatment decision.','What additional surface evidence is necessary to evaluate the request?'],
['Holiday facility staffing: confirm the handoff owner','facility-cpo','Write down who has accepted each responsibility during holiday coverage. A roster alone does not show that open incidents or maintenance concerns were transferred.','Coverage roster;Open issues;Acknowledgment record;Escalation route','This note sets no staffing ratio or qualification requirement. Use the actual venue obligations and approved operating process.','Who owns each unresolved action during the coverage period?'],
['Filter-media replacement questions: attach service history','filters-valves-plumbing','Collect the filter identity and documented service history before asking whether media should be replaced. Keep the reason for the inquiry separate from the proposed solution.','Filter model;Service history;Comparable recorded readings;Professional question','This article sets no media life or replacement threshold. It does not instruct opening or servicing a pressure vessel.','Which manufacturer information and assessment support the proposed replacement?'],
['Priming complaints after winter: a symptom record','pumps-motors','Record the exact observed behavior, its timing, and the equipment identity for the service provider. Do not turn a list of possible causes into a diagnosis.','Pump model;Exact reported behavior;Recent completed work;Observation timeline','This note gives no priming, leak-test, or restart procedure. Keep unsafe or invasive investigation with qualified personnel.','Which observation would help the service provider distinguish the reported behavior?'],
['Heater opening service: preserve winter history','heaters-heat-pumps','Attach winter observations and prior service records to the opening request. The technician should be able to distinguish known work from assumptions about storage condition.','Heater identity;Closing record;Winter concerns;Last completed service','This checklist does not authorize ignition, electrical work, or gas work. The qualified provider follows the exact instructions for the unit.','What unresolved winter concern must be reviewed before planning startup service?'],
['Cover-removal appointments: document the starting state','covers-safety-equipment','Record the cover identity and visible starting condition from accessible viewpoints. Keep the removal work scope separate from any later storage or repair request.','Cover identity;Safe overview;Known concern;Agreed service scope','This article gives no pumping, lifting, or removal procedure. Follow the applicable cover instructions and qualified service process.','Which concern changes the scope or needs manufacturer input before the appointment?'],
['Pre-inspection planning: work backward from the authority list','facility-cpo','Use the actual authority requirements to build the pre-inspection record. Assign an owner to each missing document or pending assessment.','Authority checklist;Available evidence;Missing items;Assigned owners','This article does not establish an inspection timeline or certify readiness. Resolve uncertain requirements with the responsible authority.','Which unresolved requirement prevents the operator from confirming readiness for inspection?'],
['Robot after storage: document before a service inquiry','robots-cleaners','Compare the stored equipment record with the current safe observations. Keep the cleaner and its power equipment identified so support can locate the correct instructions.','Cleaner identity;Power equipment identity;Storage record;Visible concern','This note does not instruct a first run or battery test. Use the exact manufacturer instructions and qualified support when a concern is present.','Which concern needs support review before the owner follows the operating instructions?'],
['Salt-system opening requests: preserve component history','salt-chemistry-controllers','Keep the cell, controller, and related service history in the same opening packet. Label any replacement since closing so old references are not reused silently.','Current component identities;Closing record;Replacement history;Open questions','This article gives no salt level, installation, or startup sequence. Follow the current system instructions and qualified service review.','Do the instructions and prior records still match the components now installed?'],
['Training new technicians: distinguish photo evidence from conclusions','partsnap','Teach the record first: an overview locates the equipment, a label identifies it, and a note states the unresolved question. Keep the conclusion with its supporting source.','Safe overview;Readable equipment identity;Dated observation;Source-backed conclusion if available','A photo or automated suggestion is not a diagnosis or confirmed fit. Do not invent confidence when a label cannot be read.','Can another technician trace the conclusion back to the actual evidence?'],
['The next editorial cycle: refresh sources before reuse','manuals-sources','Review the source route, document applicability, and unresolved corrections before reusing a field note. Keep the original publication date separate from a substantive update.','Official source route;Applicable document revision;Correction history;New review date','A recently accessed homepage does not validate every older statement. Narrow or remove claims that lack applicable evidence.','Which statement needs new evidence before the article is reused?']
];

export const articles = rows.map(([title, cluster, answer, fields, boundary, question], index) => {
  const date = new Date(Date.UTC(2026, 8, 29 + index)).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
  const offset = date < '2026-11-01' ? '-05:00' : '-06:00';
  const slug = title.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-|-$/g, '');
  return { id: `sl-field-${String(index + 1).padStart(3, '0')}`, title, cluster, answer,
    fields: fields.split(';'), boundary, question, date, published: `${date}T08:00:00${offset}`,
    modified: `${date}T08:00:00${offset}`, status: 'scheduled', slug,
    path: `/blog/${cluster}/${slug}/` };
});
